---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import ContactForm from "@/components/global/ContactForm.astro";
import Adventure from "../content/images/page/about/Adventure.webp";
import heyjoacimeldre from "../content/images/page/about/heyjoacimeldre.svg";

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
    title="About - Joacim Eldre"
    description="Joacim Eldre is a boy (guy?) who designs, adventure, and love most things yellow."
>
    <section>
        <div class="pt-16 max-w-xl2">
            <h1 class="typo-display-xl mb-4">
                I'm a boy, friend, dad, designer, adventurer, nerd, rainbow spewer, & human.
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                I like doing.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                Making. Designing. Drawing. Reading. Discovering. Building. Writing. Sharing. Helping. Playing. Learning. Adventuring. Laughing. Living. Loving.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                And I like to solve problems. The joy in figuring out why a thing doesn't work, and then fixing it, making it (ideally) better than before. To fine tune and adjust until whatever I'm doing is just right, when it looks and feels good.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                Or inventing something new that previously didn't exist.
            </p>
            <Image
                src={heyjoacimeldre}
                alt="A very accurate self portrait, a yellow head with two eyes and a slightly smiling mouth, one eye and a bit of the mouth is outside of the head."
                class="mt-10 w-50"
            />
            <p class="mt-10 typo-main">
                I'm formally educated as a visual designer and game designer. Throughout my life so far I've always felt at home with structure and limitation. Functional and practical systems. I think that my strongest skill is visualization, to form written language into shapes and figures. I'm a visual thinker so seeing what you're saying is very natural to me, inside my mind I'm seeing what you say as moving images. I'm fairly technical, and have a strong interest in writing. I tend to fall into what some people would call unicorn (or potato) positions at work. I'm quick at understanding how new software and hardware works, I'm a practical learner, and I ask to understand. Being curious is a core value in me.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                During most week days I design (and configure and operate, but this is the less fun part so let's not talk about that) software in public healthcare. We're working on remote patient care, and patient flow inside the hospital.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                In my spare time I spend as much time as I can with family and friends, draw, play and make video games, use my hands on crafty things like knitting and wood working, and go on adventures near and far.
            </p>
            <Image
                src={Adventure}
                alt="A photo of my son and me on a hiking adventure in a forest, I've drawn a bunch doodles around us."
                title="My son and me on an adventure"
                class="mt-12 rounded-lg mx-auto"
            />
            <h2
                class="mt-8 typo-display-lg mb-4"
            >
                I really like
            </h2>
            <ul
                class="list-disc list-inside mt-6 typo-main space-y-2"
            >
                <li>design systems.</li>
                <li>visual design.</li>
                <!-- prettier-ignore -->
                <li><span class="inline-highlight inline-highlight-chip bg-accent-50" style="--selection-highlight: var(--color-accent-50);">yellow.</span></li>
                <li>patterns.</li>
                <li>listening to rain.</li>
                <li>drawing.</li>
                <li>video games.</li>
            </ul>
            <h2 class="mt-8 typo-display-lg mb-4">
                Play
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                My kids and I like to play. The ground is lava is a favourite. A fun way to get time, and distance to pass! We step on small rocks and grass patches, and balance along fallen trees to stay alive. I think that everyone should play a lot more, be friendly to your inner child, it feels good.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                I also make tiny video games (see <a href="/posts/2026-06-12-bloob-final/">Bloob</a>, <a href="/posts/2026-07-22-shapedrifter/">Shapedrifter</a>, and <a href="/posts/2026-09-28-stack-a-snack/">Stack a Snack</a>) for my kids and me to play.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 typo-main">
                They push me to have more fun, and I love that!
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
